; The root of the scenario's world.  It delegates example. to the
; primary which serves it, and vouches for that delegation with a DS.
;
; The DS is put in by the harness: it is made of the key signing key of
; example., and that key does not exist until the primary below has
; served the zone once, so the root zone cannot be complete until then.
$ORIGIN .
$TTL 3600
@		IN	SOA	ns.root. root.root. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@		IN	NS	ns.root.
ns.root.	IN	A	{{ROOT_ADDR}}
example.	IN	NS	ns.example.
ns.example.	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
example.	IN	DS	{{DS example}}
